> sx(i: i8) = i
> wrap sx
wrap analysis of sx:
  no wrapping or rounding operations
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 256 points of the domain
> sext(x: u32) = i64(i32(x))
> wrap sext
wrap analysis of sext:
  i32(x)   (i32)
      truncates at 32557 points, e.g. x=4294967295
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 32557 points, e.g. x=4294967295
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4294967296 points); not exhaustive
> signext(x: u16) = (x xor 32768) - 32768
> wrap signext
wrap analysis of signext:
  (x xor 0x8000) - 32768   (u16)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 32768 points, e.g. x=32768
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 32768 points, e.g. x=32768
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 32768 points, e.g. x=32768
      exact for: 0..32767
  over all 65536 points of the domain
> rev4(x: u4) = ((x&1)<<3)|((x&2)<<1)|((x&4)>>1)|((x&8)>>3)
> rev4b(x: u4) = ((x&8)>>3)|((x&4)>>1)|((x&2)<<1)|((x&1)<<3)
> equiv rev4 rev4b
rev4 and rev4b are equal on the domain of rev4 (exhaustive)
> range rev4
range of rev4 -> u4:
  0..15   (16 distinct values)
  values: 0..15
  fits in u4
  over all 16 points of the domain
> maskchain(x: u32) = ((x & 0xff) + 1) & 0xff
> wrap maskchain
wrap analysis of maskchain:
  (x & 0xff) + 1   (u32)
      nuw holds (proved by intervals)
      nsw holds
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4294967296 points); not exhaustive
> range maskchain
range of maskchain -> u32:
  0..255  (sampled min/max; not a sound bound)
  fits in u8
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4294967296 points); not exhaustive
  sound bound (intervals): 0..255
